A Lojban name that looks like another expression?=A0 If there are some, we =
have a whole new set of problems, since the name-other distinction is funda=
mental.

And the predicate here created means?=A0 Presumably the composition rules s=
till applies (if not, there is yet another problem) so, lacking any other i=
nformation this means "is John-Paul" or "is John and Paul", though what {ui=
 zei pi'o} means (and why we would want it) is beyond me.

My understanding of the cumulative effect of dotside is that every *name* m=
ust be surrounded by glottal stops (which otherwise do not except between f=
inal and initial vowels, i.e., phonemically conditioned).=A0 Thus, {.paris.=
rom.} is distinct from {. paris rom.}




